    "['set system accounting radius source-address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'aaa accounting network default start-stop group radius source-address 192.168.10.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'aaa accounting network default start-stop group radius source-address 192.168.10.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\naaa accounting network default start-stop group radius source-address 192.168.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: This Cisco command configures RADIUS accounting with the specified source address, which is the equivalent functionality of the Juniper command. The \"aaa accounting network\" part enables accounting for network services, \"default\" applies it to all network services, \"start-stop\" records accounting at both start and end of sessions, and \"group radius\" specifies RADIUS as the accounting method.', 'trans_template': 'aaa accounting network default start-stop group radius source-address 192.168.10.1'}]]": 1
